cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its write-ups, please cite it as below. Code is MIT; prose is CC BY 4.0."
type: software
title: "Old algorithms, implemented"
abstract: >-
  Python implementations of algorithms from dated historical sources, each
  checked against the worked examples in the source or its oldest commentary:
  Aryabhata's kuttaka, Madhava's series for pi with its end corrections, and
  the square root of 2 on the Babylonian tablet YBC 7289.
authors:
  - family-names: Subrahmanya
    given-names: Prasad
    website: "https://prasad.tech"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/prasadus92/old-algorithms"
url: "https://prasad.tech/old-algorithms/"
keywords:
  - history of mathematics
  - Indian mathematics
  - kuttaka
  - Aryabhata
  - extended Euclidean algorithm
  - Madhava series
  - Babylonian mathematics
  - YBC 7289
